      },
      "lineNbr": 427,
      "author": {
        "id": 1135824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T09:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I remember we\u0027ve discussed this elsewhere, but don\u0027t remember the conclusion. Why can\u0027t we just have the setup code fill in the SHA256 digest for an empty buffer if no PCR binding is required? Then we don\u0027t need any special handling here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 426,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 427,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "05280b5d6a2d60ab7e8701d59d8827df3f92a30a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f168bc5_73004af8",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 35
      },
      "lineNbr": 427,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-22T13:02:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We had this discussion in the design doc. I prefer this solution because the caller doesn\u0027t have to worry about including the sha256(0) as digest in the list of criteria. Also, since we have two criteria, it would require the called to set both to 0 - sha256(0) values if they want no restrictions.",
      "parentUuid": "05cf034c_b55a9580",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 426,
        "startChar": 3,
